  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Asian Elephant Conservation Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to continue to maintain and use captive elephants for forest patrols as well as to build the capacity of the Conservation Response Unit (CRU) staff in activities such as patrolling, navigation (maps, GPS, compass etc.), human elephant conflict (HEC) mitigation tools, legal information, record keeping and monitoring. The CRUs monitor wildlife and illegal activities, respond to HEC and assess approaches to mitigate the conflicts in different sites. A community-based approach is recognized as one essential component of the program to ensure sustainable management of HEC</narrative>
  </description>
